      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Step 1: Find the weight of the two canoes.\nSince two canoes weigh a total of 56 pounds, each canoe weighs 56 / 2 = 28 pounds.\n\nStep 2: Find the weight of the three canoes.\nThe weight of the three canoes is three times the weight of one canoe, so it weighs 3 * 28 = 84 pounds.\n\nStep 3: Find the weight of the seven bowling balls.\nSince seven bowling balls weigh the same as three canoes, the weight of one bowling ball is one-seventh of the weight of the three canoes. So, one bowling ball weighs 84 / 7 = 12 pounds.\n\nTherefore, one bowling ball weighs 12 pounds.\nThe calculated answer is \\boxed{12}.",
