    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let $b$ be the weight of one bowling ball, and let $c$ be the weight of one canoe.\nWe're given that $7b = 3c$ and that $2c = 56$.\nFrom the latter equation, we can solve for $c$:\n\\begin{align*}\n2c &= 56\\\\\nc &= 28\\text{ pounds each}.\n\\end{align*}\nSubstituting $c=28$ into the former equation, we have:\n\\begin{align*}\n7b &= 3c\\\\\n7b &= 3(28)\\\\\n7b &= 84\\\\\nb &= \\frac{84}{7}\\\\\nb &= \\boxed{12}\\text{ pounds each}.\n\\end{align*}. The answer is 12",
