    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let's start by calculating the weight of one canoe with variables \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\n2x = 56\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{56}{2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = 28 \\text{ pounds}\n\\]\n\nNext, we know that seven bowling balls weigh the same as three canoes. Let's denote the weight of each canoe as \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{Weight of one canoe} = 28 \\text{ pounds}\n\\]\n\nThe combined weight for three canoes will be:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 28 = 84 \\text{ pounds}\n\\]\n\nSince seven bowling balls weigh the same as three canoes, each bowling ball should weigh:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{84}{7} = 12 \\text{ pounds}\n\\]\n\nThus, the weight of one bowling ball is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{12}\n\\]",
